---
export const title = 'Keyboard and accessibility';
export const order = 400;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  Tabs follow the WAI-ARIA tabs pattern. <code>wc-tabs</code> is the
  <code>tablist</code>, each tab is a <code>tab</code> with
  <code>aria-selected</code>, and inside a <code>wc-tab-group</code> each panel
  is a <code>tabpanel</code> labelled by its tab. The tab list is one tab stop,
  on the selected tab. Left and Right (mirrored in right-to-left layouts) move
  to the previous and next tab, Home and End to the first and last. Moving to a
  tab selects it. Disabled tabs are skipped.
</p>
<p>
  Each tab fires <code>change</code> on <code>wc-tabs</code> with
  <code>detail.index</code> and <code>detail.value</code>. With
  <code>managed</code> the tabs do not change the selection themselves: set
  <code>selected</code> on the chosen tab from the <code>change</code> listener.
</p>
<p>
  Tabs that go to other pages are navigation, not tabs. Give each one an
  <code>href</code>: it renders a plain link with <code>aria-current="page"</code>
  when selected, the list drops its <code>tablist</code> role, and you wrap it in
  a <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <nav aria-label='Account'>
    <wc-tabs variant='secondary'>
      <wc-tab href='#profile' selected>Profile</wc-tab>
      <wc-tab href='#security'>Security</wc-tab>
      <wc-tab href='#billing'>Billing</wc-tab>
    </wc-tabs>
  </nav>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Deprecated</h3>
<p>These still work through 3.x and log a console warning; 4.0 removes them.</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>active</code> on <code>wc-tab</code>: use <code>selected</code>.</li>
  <li>
    The <code>disabledreason</code> and <code>throttledelay</code> attributes
    (written <code>disabledReason</code> and <code>throttleDelay</code> in HTML):
    use <code>disabled-reason</code> and <code>throttle-delay</code>.
  </li>
  <li>The <code>tab-click</code> event: use <code>change</code>.</li>
  <li>
    Linking a panel to a tab by the tab's <code>target</code>: use
    <code>value</code>.
  </li>
</ul>
